; One name, twice, in one `fn`'s parameter list: AX3006, the code for
; two definitions of one name in one scope. Found by the seeded fuzzer
; 2026-09-27 (tests/fuzz/dup-param-llc.axfuzz): `check` said OK and the
; emitter wrote `define i64 @pick(i64 %x, i64 %x)`, which llc refuses as
; a redefinition of argument, so `build` failed at the toolchain.
;
; Parameters carry no span, so each report lands on the function's name
; and names the parameter. `_` is a name in a `fn` - `(fn (f _) _)`
; answers its argument - so `ignore` collides the same way; it died in
; llc as `%_` twice. `third` repeats one name three times and draws ONE
; report, at the second occurrence. The lambda at the end is curried by
; the parser into two nested lambdas, where the second `a` shadows the
; first, and it stays legal.
(:: pick (-> Int Int Int))
(fn (pick x x)
  x)

(:: ignore (-> Int Int Int))
(fn (ignore _ _)
  0)

(:: third (-> Int Int Int Int))
(fn (third y y y)
  y)

(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  ((lambda (a a) a) 1 2))
